Privacy Policy — Word Alert Bot
Effective date: October 7, 2026

Word Alert Bot reads message content in its configured Discord channel so
it can check for the configured word. When a match is found, it sends a
reply that mentions the configured user. The bot ignores messages sent by
bots.

The bot code does not save message contents or build a message history.
It processes messages while running to check for a match. Discord handles
the messages and mentions under Discord’s own privacy policy and terms.
The computer or hosting provider running the bot may process routine
technical connection or error logs.

The bot operator does not sell or share message contents. To ask a
question or request help with data related to the bot, contact
[your contact]. Since the bot does not store message contents, it has no
message archive to retrieve or delete.
